ion":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.heckeContinuation, ZInQ.Contrib.heckeContinuation_of_gaussPointCount, ZInQ.Contrib.heckeContinuation_functionalEquation5_of_gaussPointCount","summary":"1. Gauss's point count implies Hecke's continuation: for every natural number $d\\ne0$, $L(C_d,s)$ has an entire continuation. 2. Gauss's point count implies Hecke's continuation and the functional equation on the critical strip. 3. Hecke's continuation holds.","route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/index.html#hecke-continuation-holds"},{"id":"rank/literature/hecke/functional-equation-holds","title":"The functional equation holds","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.functionalEquation5, ZInQ.Contrib.GaussFE.literature_hecke_fe","summary":"1. Hecke's continuation for $d\\equiv5\\pmod8$ and the functional equation on the critical strip both hold. 2. The functional equation on the critical strip holds: for every squarefree natural number $d\\equiv5\\pmod8$, every entire continuation $F$ of $L(C_d,s)$ and every complex $s$ with $0<\\operatorname{Re}s<2$, $\\Lambda_{32d^2}(2-s)=-\\Lambda_{32d^2}(s)$.","route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/index.html#functional-equation-holds"},{"id":"rank/literature/hecke/row-5b-restricted","title":"Row 5b from reading A and Hecke's continuation for $d\\equiv5\\pmod8$","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.tyzRow5b_of_readingA_five","summary":"Tian–Yuan–Zhang's Theorem 3.5(2) in reading A and Hecke's continuation for $d\\equiv5\\pmod8$ together imply Tian–Yuan–Zhang's row 5b.","reading_title":{"format":"inline-parts-v1","source":"Row 5b from reading A and Hecke's continuation for $d\\equiv5\\pmod8$","parts":[["text","Row 5b from reading A and Hecke's continuation for "],["math","\\(d\\equiv5\\pmod8\\)"]]},"route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/index.html#row-5b-restricted"},{"id":"rank/literature/hecke/certified-rank-of-gauss-count","title":"CR₃^TYZ_Cl,Rk from reading A, Gross–Zagier and Gauss's point count","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.certifiedRankTYZClRk_of_elementary, ZInQ.Contrib.HeckeFE.certifiedRankTYZClRk_of_gaussPointCount","summary":"1. Assume Tian–Yuan–Zhang's Theorem 3.5(2) in reading A, the Gross–Zagier statement, Gauss's point count, and, for every squarefree $d\\equiv5\\pmod8$, that the Hecke coefficients are multiplicative and satisfy the Hecke relation at the split primes. Then the class-number hypothesis in positive-rank form CR₃^TYZ_Cl,Rk holds. 2. Reading A, the Gross–Zagier statement and Gauss's point count imply CR₃^TYZ_Cl,Rk.","route":"../roadmap/rank/literature/hecke/index.html#certified-rank-of-gauss-count"}],"result_edges":[["rank/literature/hecke/certified-rank-of-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/functional-equation-holds","rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/hecke-continuation-holds","rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/continuation-of-deuring",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/functional-equation-holds","rank/literature/hecke/continuation-of-deuring",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/functional-equation-of-deuring","rank/literature/hecke/continuation-of-deuring",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/row-5b-restricted","rank/literature/hecke/continuation-of-deuring",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/functional-equation-of-deuring",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/certified-rank-of-gauss-count","rank/literature/hecke/row-5b-restricted",0,1]],"boundary_edges":[["rank/literature/hecke/certified-rank-of-gauss-count","rank/certified-rank-tyz-cl-rk",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/certified-rank-of-gauss-count","rank/literature/certified-rank-tyz-cl-rk-of-literature",0,1],["rank/literature/hecke/both-from-gauss-count","rank/literature/functional-equation",1,0],["rank/literature/hecke/func